# nemotron-3.5-bolt on a Mac: llama.cpp with Metal, NVIDIA's own IQ2 "for size"
# GGUF (~24 GB total). HONEST WARNING: NVIDIA designed and benched this for
# NVIDIA hardware (RTX Spark / DGX Spark with llama.cpp); Apple Silicon is NOT
# in their test matrix, so this Mac path is UNPROVEN until the PROOF line is
# filled. Two specific risks:
#   - the Mamba linear layers are NVFP4 (W4A16) and no Metal NVFP4 kernel is
#     confirmed — those layers may fall back to CPU or need a newer build;
#   - vision via the mmproj on Metal is unverified — serve text first.
# The LLM backbone is NemotronHPuzzle, supported since ~llama.cpp b10776; rack
# pins b11430, so the architecture loads.
#
# 1 FIT     22.0 GB LLM (IQ2_XXS experts, Q8_0 attn/embeddings) + 1.7 GB vision
#           mmproj = ~23.75 GB. Hybrid, so KV is small (most blocks are Mamba,
#           no KV; q8_0 KV on the few attention blocks). NVIDIA designed it to
#           fit 24 GB total. Comfortable on a 48 GB+ Mac; tight on 36 GB (raise
#           iogpu.wired_limit). ~84 tok/s decode reported on an RTX Spark.
WEIGHTS_GB=23.75
# 2 ENGINE  llama.cpp at rack's pinned build (b11430), Metal.
ENGINE=llamacpp
# 3 ACCESS  NVIDIA's own GGUF conversion, pinned.
. "$RECIPE_DIR/model.env"
ARTIFACT=nvidia/NVIDIA-Nemotron-3.5-Bolt-74B-A9B-24GB-GGUF/NVIDIA-Nemotron-3.5-Bolt-74B-A9B-24GB.gguf
ARTIFACT_REVISION=e0fecb69cb3e5e4c5e8a056fa2aec98c78e91246
SERVE_ARGS=(
  # 4 SHAPE
  --n-gpu-layers 999
  --ctx-size 98304               # NVIDIA's llama.cpp recipe value; the model's window is 262144
  --flash-attn on
  --cache-type-k q8_0            # NVIDIA's recipe caches KV at q8_0
  --cache-type-v q8_0
  # 5 DIALECT
  --jinja
  --reasoning-format deepseek    # <think> spans become reasoning_content
  # VISION (unproven on Metal): the mmproj is mmproj-NVIDIA-Nemotron-3.5-Bolt-74B-A9B-24GB.gguf
  # in the same repo. To try it, pull that file and add: --mmproj <path>
)
ENV_EXTRA=()
# 8 PROOF   DOES NOT LOAD on rack's pinned llama.cpp b11430 (measured 2026-10-15):
#             check_tensor_dims: tensor 'blk.1.ffn_gate_inp.weight' has wrong
#             shape; expected 4096,496, got 4096,240
#           Cause: this is a HETEROGENEOUS "Puzzle" MoE — expert count varies per
#           layer (240/304/432). b11430's loader assumes a uniform expert count,
#           so the router tensor fails its shape check on the first layer that
#           differs. The pre-release NemotronHPuzzle support in ~b10776 does not
#           yet handle per-layer-varying experts.
#           UPDATE: llama.cpp b11675 (2026-10-16) DOES load and generate it on
#           Metal (tested ad-hoc 2026-10-15) — the loader gap closed between
#           b11430 and b11675. BUT it is SLOW: ~8.5 tok/s decode (TTFT 0.84s),
#           ~10x below a 9B-active MoE's expected Mac speed, because the NVFP4
#           Mamba layers have no Metal kernel and fall back to CPU. Bumping
#           LLAMACPP_BUILD to >= b11675 (shared with the Spark/Linux paths) would
#           let rack serve it, but the GGUF is not fast on a Mac. For a fast Mac
#           number use the MLX path instead: rapid-mlx 4-bit (requantized, NO
#           NVFP4, text-only, ~43 GB, needs the Rapid-MLX tool, not stock mlx-lm).
